  LAMBDA-8 REBUILT FROM THE SEVEN CONSTRAINTS THE BOOK PRINTS

  1. DO THE SEVEN GENERATE THE OBJECT?
       l <= n-1    relates n and l
       k <= 4l+2   relates l and k
       q <= k      relates k and q
       f <= e-1    relates e and f
       g <= 4f+2   relates f and g
       g <= q      relates q and g
       2S <= k     relates k and 2S
     seated tower-2.py L8()   976 cells
     rebuilt from the seven   976 cells
     identical cell for cell  True
     redundant constraints    none -- every one is needed
     So the constraint set is exactly seven: seven generate it, and no six do.

  2. THE CONSTRAINT GRAPH
     8 nodes, 7 edges: l-n · k-l · k-q · e-f · f-g · g-q · 2S-k
     a tree? True   (1 component(s), 7 edges over 8 nodes)

  3. THE TRIPLE CENSUS, over all C(7,3) = 35 triples of constraints
     triples spanning 4 nodes: 7
     triples spanning 5 nodes: 20
     triples spanning 6 nodes: 8
     total 35;  3-bodies 0

  4. ONE EDGE FROM A 3-BODY
     add 2S - l   -> a 3-body on {2S, k, l}
     add 2S - q   -> a 3-body on {2S, k, q}
     add e - g   -> a 3-body on {e, f, g}
     add f - q   -> a 3-body on {f, g, q}
     add g - k   -> a 3-body on {g, k, q}
     add k - n   -> a 3-body on {k, l, n}
     add l - q   -> a 3-body on {k, l, q}
     7 places, one per existing edge, which is what adding an edge
     to a tree gives.

  VERDICT ON CANDIDATE E-072
